@id: scene.047_mika
@when: Unknown.scene_047_mika
@where: Realm/Physical/Unknown
@scope: narrative
@entities: [Celly, Geralt, Mika, Zephyr]
@region: Unknown
@environment: wasteland
@terrain_family: wasteland
@spatial_scale_hint: massive

=segments:
  - line: 1
    type: narration
    text: "book 8"
  - line: 2
    type: narration
    text: "chapter 047-mika"
  - line: 4
    type: narration
    text: "~~~THE HOMECOMING~~~~"
  - line: 5
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 1: RETURN THROUGH SCORCH"
  - line: 7
    type: narration
    text: "The desert remembered them."
  - line: 8
    type: narration
    text: "The Scorch breathed its dry, ancient breath over the column of four hundred and sixty souls as they marched eastward."
  - line: 9
    type: narration
    text: "They were a patchwork army—two hundred and ten Legion veterans moving with the stiff, automatic gait of soldiers who had marched to hell and back, and two hundred and fifty freed slaves, their steps uneven but fierce with new purpose."
  - line: 10
    type: narration
    text: "The heat shimmered above the salt flats, distorting the memories of blood and battle into wavering ghosts."
  - line: 12
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt walked at the head, his Stage 1 wings folded tight against his back."
  - line: 13
    type: narration
    text: "They caught the sun, casting a jagged, dragon-shaped shadow that stretched ahead of him like a guide."
  - line: 14
    type: narration
    text: "Mika walked at his side, her eyes perpetually scanning the horizon, a habit war had etched into her bones."
  - line: 15
    type: narration
    text: "They spoke little."
  - line: 16
    type: narration
    text: "The silence between them was not empty; it was full of the unspoken understanding that the mission was over, and the weight of what came next was settling upon them."
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "Weeks bled into one another, marked by the twin suns rising and setting over the endless ochre wastes."
  - line: 19
    type: narration
    text: "They followed the Star Needle's faint resonance in Geralt's bones, a homing pulse pulling them toward the crash site, toward the place this had all begun."
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "Then, one morning, they saw it."
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "A smudge on the horizon resolved into walls."
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "Real, constructed walls of fitted stone, rising from the mountain's scar."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "Smoke curled from chimneys."
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "The skeletal wreckage of the Anunnaki ship was still visible, but now it was integrated—girders repurposed as support beams, hull plating forming roofs."
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "Life had taken root in the wound."
  - line: 29
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"Ironspire,\""
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "They approached slowly, a massive column emerging from the desert."
  - line: 32
    type: narration
    text: "Sentries on the walls spotted them, and a cry went up—not of alarm, but of recognition."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "The gates swung open."
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "Celly Sundrift met them just inside, her hands covered in brick-dust, her face older and wiser than when they'd last seen her at the collapsing Hub Needle."
  - line: 36
    type: narration
    text: "\"Commander."
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt.\" Her eyes took in the wings, the army of freed souls behind them, and a slow smile spread across her face."
  - line: 38
    type: narration
    text: "\"You did it."
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "You actually did it.\""
  - line: 41
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"We did,\""
  - line: 43
    type: narration
    text: "Celly ushered them in, calling for water and food to be brought for the weary travelers."
  - line: 44
    type: narration
    text: "The town was a marvel of pragmatic beauty."
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "Stone houses with metal-reinforced doors."
  - line: 46
    type: narration
    text: "A central well with a clever pulley system."
  - line: 47
    type: narration
    text: "Workshops humming with activity."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "Fields of hardy, genetically-modified crops growing in terraced plots against the mountain."
  - line: 49
    type: narration
    text: "It was alive."
  - line: 51
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"Where are the founders?\""
  - line: 53
    type: narration
    text: "Celly's smile turned wry."
  - line: 54
    type: narration
    text: "\"Sleeping.\""
  - line: 56
    type: narration
    text: "She led them to a sturdy longhouse near the center of town."
  - line: 57
    type: narration
    text: "Inside, in a room filled with maps and building plans, two men were sprawled on cots."
  - line: 58
    type: narration
    text: "Roric and Kael."
  - line: 59
    type: narration
    text: "Deep in sleep, mouths slightly open, utterly dead to the world."
  - line: 61
    type: narration
    text: "Celly walked over."
  - line: 62
    type: narration
    text: "\"Roric?"
  - line: 63
    type: narration
    text: "Company.\" Nothing."
  - line: 64
    type: narration
    text: "She shook his shoulder."
  - line: 65
    type: narration
    text: "\"Roric."
  - line: 66
    type: narration
    text: "Wake up.\" A snore."
  - line: 67
    type: narration
    text: "Finally, she kicked the leg of the cot."
  - line: 68
    type: narration
    text: "\"RORIC!"
  - line: 69
    type: narration
    text: "THE ARMY'S HERE!\""
  - line: 71
    type: narration
    text: "Roric snorted, rolled over, and continued sleeping."
  - line: 72
    type: narration
    text: "Kael didn't even twitch."
  - line: 74
    type: narration
    text: "Celly shrugged, turning back to Geralt and Mika."
  - line: 75
    type: narration
    text: "\"They do this."
  - line: 76
    type: narration
    text: "Work themselves into the ground for days, then crash for twelve hours straight."
  - line: 77
    type: narration
    text: "Sleep like the dead.\" She paused, a flicker of memory crossing her face."
  - line: 78
    type: narration
    text: "\"Some things never change, huh?\""
  - line: 80
    type: narration
    text: "Mika felt a strange, warm weight in her chest."
  - line: 81
    type: narration
    text: "She remembered Zephyr's report, years ago now: They slept through a spaceship crash."
  - line: 82
    type: narration
    text: "Here, in safety, they still slept through an army's homecoming."
  - line: 84
    type: narration
    text: "Celly gave them a tour as the Legion and freed slaves integrated, some finding family among Ironspire's population, others simply collapsing in grateful exhaustion."
  - line: 85
    type: narration
    text: "The settlement was more than just survival; it was a community."
  - line: 86
    type: narration
    text: "A school was being planned."
  - line: 87
    type: narration
    text: "A infirmary already running."
  - line: 89
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Celly
    text: "\"More survivors keep arriving,\""
  - line: 91
    type: narration
    text: "She led them to the western edge of town, where the mountain scar deepened."
  - line: 92
    type: narration
    text: "A team was there, carefully excavating something massive and metallic from the rock."
  - line: 93
    type: narration
    text: "\"We found this a few months back."
  - line: 94
    type: narration
    text: "Been buried for... we don't know."
  - line: 95
    type: narration
    text: "Millennia?"
  - line: 96
    type: narration
    text: "It's big."
  - line: 97
    type: narration
    text: "Feels important."
  - line: 98
    type: narration
    text: "Gives off a low hum.\""
  - line: 100
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt it immediately through his connection to Luminaire's Echo—a dormant network node, a piece of the ancient Void Spire infrastructure, sleeping beneath the earth."
  - line: 101
    type: narration
    text: "He exchanged a look with Mika."
  - line: 102
    type: narration
    text: "Another anchor point."
  - line: 104
    type: narration
    text: "They stayed for three days."
  - line: 105
    type: narration
    text: "Some of the freed slaves chose to remain in Ironspire, their fight done, craving simple walls and steady work."
  - line: 106
    type: narration
    text: "Some Legion veterans, too weary for another march, integrated into the town's guard."
  - line: 107
    type: narration
    text: "The core group that gathered to move on was smaller, tighter: Geralt, Mika, Oreck, and about fifty of the most loyal, restless veterans."
  - line: 109
    type: narration
    text: "They left at dawn, passing through Ironspire's gates and making the short trek to the nearby Star Needle Spire."
  - line: 110
    type: narration
    text: "It stood where Geralt had first returned from the Nexus, humming softly."
  - line: 111
    type: narration
    text: "From there, they picked up an old, faint trail leading north and east, into the rocky foothills."
  - line: 113
    type: narration
    text: "The path was familiar in Geralt's bones."
  - line: 114
    type: narration
    text: "He had walked it alone, bleeding and desperate, years ago."
  - line: 116
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 2: THE FALCON RIDGE FOUNDING"
  - line: 118
    type: narration
    text: "They reached the plateau by midday."
  - line: 119
    type: narration
    text: "The air was thinner here, cooler."
  - line: 120
    type: narration
    text: "The place was unremarkable—just a flat stretch of wind-scoured stone between two ridges—but both Geralt and Mika stopped as if struck."
  - line: 122
    type: narration
    text: "Mika walked to a particular depression in the rock, her boots scuffing the stone."
  - line: 123
    type: narration
    text: "\"I fell here,\" she said, her voice quiet."
  - line: 124
    type: narration
    text: "\"I was following your blood."
  - line: 125
    type: narration
    text: "I thought it was leading me to you."
  - line: 126
    type: narration
    text: "I collapsed right here.\""
  - line: 128
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt moved a few meters to the east, to a patch of darker stone."
  - line: 129
    type: narration
    text: "\"I fell here first."
  - line: 130
    type: narration
    text: "Before you ever came looking."
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "The Nexus spat me out."
  - line: 132
    type: narration
    text: "I crawled this far before I passed out.\""
  - line: 134
    type: narration
    text: "They stood in silence, the space between them suddenly charged with the ghost of those terrible, lonely hours."
  - line: 135
    type: narration
    text: "They had been meters apart, each unconscious, each believing the other was lost forever."
  - line: 136
    type: narration
    text: "The distance felt vast and insignificant all at once."
  - line: 138
    type: narration
    text: "Then, a cry from above."
  - line: 140
    type: narration
    text: "Three falcons circled against the hard blue sky."
  - line: 141
    type: narration
    text: "They were the same ones—Mika knew it in her gut."
  - line: 142
    type: narration
    text: "They wheeled once, twice, then dove sharply beyond the northern rise."
  - line: 144
    type: narration
    text: "Mika and Geralt looked at each other."
  - line: 146
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"Again?\""
  - line: 148
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"Again,\""
  - line: 150
    type: narration
    text: "They followed, their small company trailing behind."
  - line: 151
    type: narration
    text: "They crested the rise—"
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "—and the valley opened below them."
  - line: 155
    type: narration
    text: "It was hidden, perfectly sheltered by the surrounding ridges."
  - line: 156
    type: narration
    text: "A clear stream cut through its center, fed by a waterfall that cascaded from the eastern cliff."
  - line: 157
    type: narration
    text: "Ancient, gnarled trees dotted the slopes, and the floor was rich, dark soil."
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "It was a bowl of life carved into the stone desert."
  - line: 160
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"The place we missed by fifty meters,\""
  - line: 162
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt pointed."
  - line: 163
    type: narration
    text: "High on the cliff face, beneath the falcons' now-visible nest, a scrap of fabric fluttered."
  - line: 164
    type: narration
    text: "Mika scrambled up the loose scree, her heart pounding."
  - line: 165
    type: narration
    text: "She pulled it free."
  - line: 167
    type: narration
    text: "It was the scarf."
  - line: 168
    type: narration
    text: "Her scarf."
  - line: 169
    type: narration
    text: "The one she'd lost years ago on this very plateau, the one with the ambiguous, blood-stained pattern that could be a falcon or a dragon."
  - line: 170
    type: narration
    text: "It was sun-faded, but the stain was still there."
  - line: 171
    type: narration
    text: "His blood."
  - line: 172
    type: narration
    text: "Her history."
  - line: 174
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"How is this here?\""
  - line: 175
    type: narration
    text: "she breathed."
  - line: 177
    type: narration
    text: "No answer came."
  - line: 178
    type: narration
    text: "The wind sighed through the valley."
  - line: 179
    type: narration
    text: "Some rhymes in reality had no reason, only resonance."
  - line: 181
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt climbed up to join her."
  - line: 182
    type: narration
    text: "He took the scarf from her trembling hands."
  - line: 183
    type: narration
    text: "He found a straight, strong branch from a fallen tree."
  - line: 184
    type: narration
    text: "With careful, deliberate movements, he tied the scarf to one end."
  - line: 185
    type: narration
    text: "He carried it down into the heart of the valley, to where the stream entered from the north."
  - line: 186
    type: narration
    text: "He drove the branch deep into the earth."
  - line: 188
    type: narration
    text: "The makeshift banner caught the breeze, the faded fabric snapping once, then settling."
  - line: 190
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"Welcome to Falcon Ridge,\""
  - line: 192
    type: narration
    text: "And they began to build."
  - line: 194
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 3: EARLY DAYS"
  - line: 196
    type: narration
    text: "Month 1 was raw survival."
  - line: 197
    type: narration
    text: "They cleared a flat space near the stream with axes and sheer will."
  - line: 198
    type: narration
    text: "The first structure was a simple hut of stone and timber—Geralt and Mika's."
  - line: 199
    type: narration
    text: "The second was a long barracks for the soldiers."
  - line: 200
    type: narration
    text: "It was basic, drafty, and home."
  - line: 202
    type: narration
    text: "Month 2 brought order."
  - line: 203
    type: narration
    text: "Merra Sundrift arrived from Ironspire with a caravan of seeds, tools, and stubborn hope."
  - line: 204
    type: narration
    text: "She walked the south-facing slope with Mika, pointing where the sun would linger."
  - line: 205
    type: narration
    text: "They planted the first fields."
  - line: 206
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt and the veterans channeled the stream, creating irrigation ditches with precise, military efficiency."
  - line: 207
    type: narration
    text: "A storage cache was dug into a cool hillside."
  - line: 209
    type: narration
    text: "Month 3 saw the valley become a settlement."
  - line: 210
    type: narration
    text: "More veterans arrived from Ironspire, their war ended, seeking the quiet company of their commanders."
  - line: 211
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck took charge of construction, his methodical, powerful presence perfect for lifting stone beams and plotting defensive lines."
  - line: 212
    type: narration
    text: "A low perimeter wall began to snake around the valley's most accessible approaches."
  - line: 214
    type: narration
    text: "The valley's strategic perfection was undeniable."
  - line: 215
    type: narration
    text: "It overlooked the only easy approach."
  - line: 216
    type: narration
    text: "The Star Needle Spire was a clear silhouette on the western horizon, a constant and comforting landmark."
  - line: 217
    type: narration
    text: "They had a two-mile sightline—any approaching threat would be seen with hours of warning."
  - line: 219
    type: narration
    text: "One morning, as Mika inspected the growing wall, she turned and found Zephyr standing beside her, as if he'd been there for hours."
  - line: 220
    type: narration
    text: "He was studying the masonry."
  - line: 222
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Perimeter's good,\""
  - line: 223
    type: narration
    text: "the ancient Sage said, not looking at her. \"Won't stop me, though.\""
  - line: 225
    type: narration
    text: "Then he was gone, leaving only the scent of ozone and timelessness."
  - line: 227
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 4: THE FIRST TONGUE"
  - line: 229
    type: narration
    text: "A year had gentled Falcon Ridge."
  - line: 230
    type: narration
    text: "The fields were green."
  - line: 231
    type: narration
    text: "The huts had become houses."
  - line: 232
    type: narration
    text: "The archive was Mika's pride—a solid stone building with a vaulted ceiling, filled with empty shelves waiting for knowledge."
  - line: 234
    type: narration
    text: "One evening, Geralt, Mika, and Zephyr sat by the central fire."
  - line: 235
    type: narration
    text: "The conversation drifted, as it often did with Zephyr, toward the deep past."
  - line: 237
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Zephyr
    text: "\"The First Tongue isn't spoken,\""
  - line: 239
    type: narration
    text: "Mika leaned forward."
  - line: 240
    type: narration
    text: "\"The language of creation?\""
  - line: 242
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"One of them. The one this world was sung in.\""
  - line: 243
    type: narration
    text: "He looked at her, his ancient eyes reflecting the fire. \"Would you like to hear a word?\""
  - line: 245
    type: narration
    text: "She nodded."
  - line: 247
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Zephyr
    text: "\"Sek'han,\""
  - line: 249
    type: narration
    text: "Mika looked at a fist-sized stone near her foot."
  - line: 250
    type: narration
    text: "She focused, not on moving it with force, but on introducing the concept of sek'han to it."
  - line: 251
    type: narration
    text: "She didn't speak aloud."
  - line: 252
    type: narration
    text: "She let the meaning form in her mind, in her will."
  - line: 254
    type: narration
    text: "The stone lifted."
  - line: 255
    type: narration
    text: "Smoothly."
  - line: 256
    type: narration
    text: "Silently."
  - line: 257
    type: narration
    text: "Three feet into the air, where it hung, turning slowly."
  - line: 259
    type: narration
    text: "Mika stared at it, then at her hand."
  - line: 260
    type: narration
    text: "There had been no strain."
  - line: 261
    type: narration
    text: "No epic struggle."
  - line: 262
    type: narration
    text: "It had felt... obvious."
  - line: 263
    type: narration
    text: "Like recalling a melody she'd forgotten she knew."
  - line: 265
    type: narration
    text: "Zephyr was staring at her, his usual placidity replaced by sharp, assessing interest."
  - line: 266
    type: narration
    text: "\"That,\" he said slowly, \"should have taken months of meditation."
  - line: 267
    type: narration
    text: "Years, for most.\""
  - line: 269
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"It felt natural,\""
  - line: 271
    type: narration
    text: "That night, by candlelight in the archive, Mika took out a blank ledger."
  - line: 272
    type: narration
    text: "Her hand did not shake."
  - line: 273
    type: narration
    text: "\"I need to document this,\" she said to Geralt, who watched from the doorway."
  - line: 274
    type: narration
    text: "\"Before I forget how easy it felt.\""
  - line: 276
    type: narration
    text: "She titled the first page: On Resonance and Intent."
  - line: 277
    type: narration
    text: "And she began to write."
  - line: 279
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 5: TIME PASSING"
  - line: 281
    type: narration
    text: "Year 2."
  - line: 282
    type: narration
    text: "The archive grew, its shelves filling with Mika's precise handwriting."
  - line: 283
    type: narration
    text: "The Needle Spire on the horizon began to glow with a soft, steady light at night."
  - line: 284
    type: narration
    text: "Drawn by its energy, a new settlement sprang up at its base—the Sundrift family and other pioneers, building a community of engineers and mystics."
  - line: 285
    type: narration
    text: "Falcon Ridge remained smaller, a place of quiet study and green growth."
  - line: 287
    type: narration
    text: "Year 3."
  - line: 288
    type: narration
    text: "Zephyr became a regular visitor, though never a resident."
  - line: 289
    type: narration
    text: "He and Mika would spend hours in the archive, her writing, him offering corrections that felt less like instruction and more like reminders."
  - line: 290
    type: narration
    text: "\"The word for 'binding' has a secondary resonance for 'healing,' but only if your heart- tone is in the minor key,\" he'd say, and she would nod, scribbling in the margin."
  - line: 291
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt learned by osmosis, the concepts weaving into his understanding of the dragon armor's power."
  - line: 293
    type: narration
    text: "Year 4."
  - line: 294
    type: narration
    text: "From the ridge, they could see Ironspire's expansion—new walls, watchtowers, the smoke of industry."
  - line: 295
    type: narration
    text: "Trade caravans now moved regularly between the two settlements and the Sundrift Spire-town."
  - line: 296
    type: narration
    text: "Falcon Ridge supplied rare herbs and knowledge; Ironspire provided metalwork and grain; the Spire-town offered technical skill."
  - line: 297
    type: narration
    text: "A fragile, thriving network."
  - line: 299
    type: narration
    text: "Year 5."
  - line: 300
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck stood at the valley entrance at dawn, a pack on his back."
  - line: 301
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt and Mika came to see him off."
  - line: 303
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I'm not built for quiet,\""
  - line: 304
    type: narration
    text: "the massive man said, his voice still layered with the faint hum of his Anunnaki augmentations."
  - line: 306
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"Where will you go?\""
  - line: 308
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Somewhere that needs defending. Somewhere that needs... action.\""
  - line: 309
    type: narration
    text: "He looked at Mika. \"Thank you. For everything.\""
  - line: 311
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"You saved us as much as we saved you,\""
  - line: 313
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We're even, then.\""
  - line: 314
    type: narration
    text: "He turned and walked down the path, into the rising sun. He never returned. The valley felt quieter, more peaceful, and somehow less complete without his solid, restless presence."
  - line: 316
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 6: THE QUIET YEARS"
  - line: 318
    type: narration
    text: "Year 6."
  - line: 319
    type: narration
    text: "An evening in late autumn."
  - line: 320
    type: narration
    text: "The fire was low."
  - line: 321
    type: narration
    text: "Zephyr was away on one of his endless walks."
  - line: 322
    type: narration
    text: "The soldiers, now farmers and builders, had long since learned to give their commanders this evening silence."
  - line: 324
    type: narration
    text: "Mika was sixty-three."
  - line: 325
    type: narration
    text: "Her hair was fully silver, her face lined with smiles and sorrows in equal measure."
  - line: 326
    type: narration
    text: "She watched the embers die, her hand resting on the completed, massive tome in her lap—The First Tongue: A Primer for Those Who Would Speak Creation."
  - line: 328
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"The book's done,\""
  - line: 330
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt sat beside her."
  - line: 331
    type: narration
    text: "Time had not touched him."
  - line: 332
    type: narration
    text: "The scars that crisscrossed his skin were as stark as the day he’d earned them."
  - line: 333
    type: narration
    text: "His face, though hardened by millennia of memory, bore no new lines."
  - line: 334
    type: narration
    text: "\"I know\" he said"
  - line: 336
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I'm done.\""
  - line: 338
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I know.\""
  - line: 340
    type: narration
    text: "The silence that followed was full and final."
  - line: 341
    type: narration
    text: "The stars above Falcon Ridge were impossibly bright."
  - line: 343
    type: narration
    text: "She went to bed first."
  - line: 344
    type: narration
    text: "He kissed her forehead, the gesture worn smooth by decades of repetition."
  - line: 346
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"See you tomorrow,\""
  - line: 348
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"See you tomorrow,\""
  - line: 350
    type: narration
    text: "She did not wake in the morning."
  - line: 352
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 7: AFTER"
  - line: 354
    type: narration
    text: "Weeks later, Geralt walked through the bustling streets of Ironspire alone."
  - line: 355
    type: narration
    text: "He carried a large, cloth-wrapped package."
  - line: 356
    type: narration
    text: "The town was noise and life—children shouting, blacksmiths hammering, the smell of baking bread."
  - line: 357
    type: narration
    text: "At the center of town stood the new library, a grand structure of stone and glass, Celly Sundrift's greatest project."
  - line: 359
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt entered the hushed interior."
  - line: 360
    type: narration
    text: "Sunlight streamed through high windows onto a central pedestal of polished black stone."
  - line: 361
    type: narration
    text: "He approached, unwrapped the package, and placed the book upon it."
  - line: 363
    type: narration
    text: "THE FIRST TONGUE: A PRIMER FOR THOSE WHO WOULD SPEAK CREATION"
  - line: 364
    type: narration
    text: "By Mika Covenant"
  - line: 366
    type: narration
    text: "He opened it to the first page, where her dedication was written in a firm, elegant hand: For those who come after."
  - line: 367
    type: narration
    text: "May you build with kinder words."
  - line: 369
    type: narration
    text: "He left it there, for the scholars, the seekers, the next generation."
  - line: 371
    type: narration
    text: "He walked back through the gates, nodding to guards who saluted him with deep respect."
  - line: 372
    type: narration
    text: "At the growing Sundrift settlement around the Needle Spire, he stopped at a market stall."
  - line: 373
    type: narration
    text: "He bought a loaf of dark bread and, from a small garden plot, a bunch of late-blooming blueflowers."
  - line: 375
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"For Mika,\""
  - line: 376
    type: narration
    text: "he told the gardener, a young woman with Merra's eyes."
  - line: 378
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"She'd like those,\""
  - line: 379
    type: narration
    text: "the girl said softly."
  - line: 381
    type: narration
    text: "He walked the now-familiar path up to Falcon Ridge."
  - line: 382
    type: narration
    text: "He left the bread on the porch of their hut—one of the veterans would find it."
  - line: 383
    type: narration
    text: "He continued to the valley entrance, where the banner still flew."
  - line: 384
    type: narration
    text: "The scarf was threadbare now, the bloodstain faded to a rust-colored whisper, the pattern forever ambiguous."
  - line: 386
    type: narration
    text: "Beside it was a simple stone marker."
  - line: 388
    type: narration
    text: "MIKA COVENANT"
  - line: 389
    type: narration
    text: "Commander."
  - line: 390
    type: narration
    text: "Scholar."
  - line: 391
    type: narration
    text: "Wife."
  - line: 392
    type: narration
    text: "She Followed Falcons Home."
  - line: 394
    type: narration
    text: "He placed the blueflowers against the cool stone."
  - line: 395
    type: narration
    text: "He sat beside the grave, his wings a dark mantle around him."
  - line: 396
    type: narration
    text: "He watched the valley—the stream she’d charted, the trees they’d planted together, the quiet industry of the home they’d built."
  - line: 397
    type: narration
    text: "The mission was complete."
  - line: 398
    type: narration
    text: "The life had been lived."
  - line: 399
    type: narration
    text: "The love had been earned."
  - line: 401
    type: narration
    text: "Through the bond, carried on Luminaire's distant, eternal Echo, a faint impression brushed his mind, clear and sure: She mattered."
  - line: 403
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt closed his eyes."
  - line: 404
    type: narration
    text: "\"I know.\""
  - line: 406
    type: narration
    text: "When he opened them, Zephyr was sitting beside him."
  - line: 407
    type: narration
    text: "He hadn't heard him approach."
  - line: 409
    type: narration
    text: "The Sage looked at the grave, then at the weathered book in the distance, then at Geralt."
  - line: 410
    type: narration
    text: "\"The teaching is preserved,\" he said."
  - line: 411
    type: narration
    text: "\"The knowledge is safe."
  - line: 412
    type: narration
    text: "Her work is done.\""
  - line: 414
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt looked at the setting sun, painting Falcon Ridge in amber and violet."
  - line: 415
    type: narration
    text: "\"What now?\""
  - line: 417
    type: narration
    text: "Zephyr stood, extending a hand."
  - line: 418
    type: narration
    text: "\"Now,\" he said, his voice holding the weight of coming eons, \"we prepare you.\""
  - line: 420
    type: narration
    text: "end of chapter 047-mika"

